WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.200 align:start position:0%
 
Oh  if you had the chance to play the Ghost  Recon wildlands beta this weekend you  probably found plenty of things you  liked and other things you didn't like  here are some things we'd like to see  added or fixed before the game launches  on march seven and if you didn't get a  chance to play the beta or you're still  on the fence about this one make sure to  hit that subscribe button so you'll be  the first to know when our review drops  next month number one alternative  chopper controls helicopters and planes  are the most efficient way of getting  around the map unfortunately flying  around in one of these birds doesn't  feel all that great your helicopter  should maintain momentum as you soar  through the skies however instead of a  smooth trip from point A to B the whole  experience felt a bit jerky when I  finally did slow down to land or to  hover it felt like the chopper was  fighting against me every step of the  way also why are there no crosshairs on  the helicopters with guns how is anyone  supposed to aim this to improve squad  commands Ghost Recon wildlands seems to  be missing a lot of squad commands that  we've come to expect in a ghost recon  game stay there especially for those of  us who don't want to play co-op I get  that this is an effort to streamline the  experience but when would I ever want my  squad to march into a hostile base  without me giving the okay first let me  set waypoints for my AI squad mates and  give me the option to tell them to stay  in the Humvee and cover me from a  mounted minigun when I want them to  number three improved no HUD mode my  favorite way to play The Ghost Recon  wildlands beta was with the HUD turned  off I found this to be way more  immersive it forced me to pay closer  attention to my surroundings and listen  to the chatter between my squad mates  and enemies  tango school start locals unfortunately  getting anywhere without a HUD is almost  impossible without constantly checking  the map in the menus I would love it if  my ghost had an in-game compass or map  that I could check similar to what we  saw in Far Cry 2 number 40 Inge sniper  rifles one cool addition to Ghost Recon  wildlands is bullet drop for long-range  firearms target down in the beta there  was a rangefinder but I wasn't able to  zero in my scopes if you're going to add  bullet drop in a tactical shooter why  not take that extra step and let us plan  the perfect shot by adding a sniper  spotter mechanic number five more  destruction I think it's probably a bit  too late to expect a destruction engine  similar to what we saw in battlefield  one but I can't tell you how many times  I drove into small trees are fences  expecting them to break and they didn't  or if they did my car would slam to a  halt first it was really annoying I'd  love it if the destruction was taken one  step further and allowed us to level  watchtowers it seems like a bit of a  stretch but right now the only way to  deal with snipers and towers is by  counter sniping them a little more  variety would be nice Ghost Recon  wildlands is out in a few weeks let me  know what you thought of the beta in the  comments below and what you think needs  to be changed or added if you want to  see more Ghost Recon wildlands check out  our no HUD gameplay and don't forget to  subscribe thanks for watching  interrogate hostile lieutenants talk to  civvies whatever it takes we'll turn  over every Rock  you  you

